'''Andromeda XIV''' ('''And XIV''') is a small satellite of the [[Andromeda Galaxy]] classed as a [[Dwarf spheroidal galaxy|dwarf spheroidal]] galaxy.<ref name=":0">{{Cite journal |last=Majewski |first=Steven R. |last2=Beaton |first2=Rachael L. |last3=Patterson |first3=Richard J. |last4=Kalirai |first4=Jasonjot S. |last5=Geha |first5=Marla C. |last6=Muñoz |first6=Ricardo R. |last7=Seigar |first7=Marc S. |last8=Guhathakurta |first8=Puragra |last9=Gilbert |first9=Karoline M. |last10=Rich |first10=R. Michael |last11=Bullock |first11=James S. |last12=Reitzel |first12=David B. |date=November 2007 |title=Discovery of Andromeda XIV: A Dwarf Spheroidal Dynamical Rogue in the Local Group? |url=https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2007ApJ...670L...9M/abstract |journal=The Astrophysical Journal |language=en |volume=670 |issue=1 |pages=L9–L12 |doi=10.1086/524033 |issn=0004-637X|arxiv=astro-ph/0702635 }}</ref>

It has an extreme speed of 481 kilometers per second placing this galaxy at the [[escape velocity]] of the Andromeda Galaxy. This would mean that this galaxy is not part of the [[Local Group]] of galaxies and is instead an isolated dwarf galaxy just passing through.<ref name=":0" />

